# AgentForge
<!-- impeccable:product-schema 1 -->

## Platform
web

## Users
Developers and builders handing off research and coding tasks while retaining approval control (confirmed by the user).

## Product Purpose
A conversational workspace for researching, writing and running code, and reviewing repository changes.

## Operating Context
Next.js web frontend and Python API. GitHub sign-in and optional repository connection are separate flows. Local installations support a bootstrap token.

## Capabilities and Constraints
Preserve the existing authenticated workspace, routing, approval modes, persistent sandbox, delivery controls and session behavior. Public claims must reflect current source. Ask me and Approve for me are distinct modes; do not imply approval is mandatory in both.

## Brand Commitments
AgentForge. Premium, minimal public landing and sign-in pages with generated background imagery. User pinned the Conductor screenshot and website as the visual reference: near black, ASCII atmosphere, compact hero, large product preview. Preserve AgentForge branding, truthful claims and unrelated changes.

## Evidence on Hand
Current source, offline tests, and explicitly illustrative conversation previews. No supplied customers, testimonials or performance benchmarks.
